// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 8 (Impl-L): GC scoping — the lane→lane
// discharge. A ref to a lane-backed binding ('lane_a', the explicit
// `lane_alloc` pin) stored into a lane-backed destination ('lane_b'):
// both sides live in the lane-bytes memory category (W2A §1.4) — the
// lane owns its own references and rewinds them together at its extent,
// so E-GC-IN-LANE must NOT fire, and the program runs.
//
// The second print proves the stores really landed on lane 2 (its
// watermark is non-zero) — the lane knows about its own.

fn main() {
    ptr lane_a = lane_alloc(2, 64)
    ptr lane_b = lane_alloc(2, 64)
    lane_b = address(lane_a)
    print(lane_used(2) > 0)
}
